---
import { site } from "../site";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How is it different from a transactional email API?",
    a: `Those are built to send receipts; receiving is an add-on that forwards raw mail. send0 starts from the inbox: messages are parsed, threaded and checked, codes are extracted, and your agent replies in the same thread.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Will sites block send0.email addresses as disposable?",
    a: `We work to make sure they don't. Every send0.email inbox belongs to a verified account, and we never market it as throwaway mail. Need your own domain? Self-host today; custom domains are coming to paid cloud plans.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How do you keep agents safe from malicious email?",
    a: `Every message carries SPF, DKIM and DMARC results and a prompt-injection flag. The MCP server hands bodies to the model as untrusted data. Approval mode puts a person before every send, and keys can be limited to one inbox.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does <span class="nb">AGPL-3.0</span> mean for me?',
    a: `Calling the API puts no obligations on your code, and you can self-host commercially. Change the server and offer it to others over a network, and you share those changes. The SDKs and MCP server are MIT.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap layout">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow">
        <b>08</b> Questions
      </span>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="h2">
        What people ask us.
      </h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Ask us anything:{" "}
        <a class="link" href={`mailto:${site.email.hello}`}>
          {site.email.hello}
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="list">
      {faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <details name="faq" open={i === 0}>
          <summary>
            <span set:html={f.q} />
            <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
          </summary>
          <div class="answer" set:html={f.a} />
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 36px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
      gap: 72px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  details:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px 2px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font: 600 19px/1.3 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  summary :global(.nb) {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  summary span:first-child {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    color: var(--ink);
    transition:
      transform 0.25s ease,
      background-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 11px;
    height: 1.75px;
    background: currentColor;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }
  .plus::after {
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
  }
  /* Answers open and close smoothly where the browser supports animating to height: auto. */
  details::details-content {
    height: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    transition:
      height 0.35s var(--ease-out),
      content-visibility 0.35s allow-discrete;
  }
  details[open]::details-content {
    height: auto;
  }
  details[open] .plus {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    background: var(--accent-tint);
  }
  .answer {
    padding: 0 48px 24px 2px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .answer :global(a) {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule);
  }
</style>
